1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,140
When I wake up, I let out a sigh. Somewhere along the way, that became a habit of mine.

2
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:22,660
I was so sure that love was supposed to be more fun than this.

3
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:02,720
Wow, you're exactly on time.

4
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:06,760
I didn't realize that you got here early. Sorry.

5
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:07,880
It's fine.

6
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:18,720
I'm sure that the next thing that happens will be me getting rejected.

7
00:02:18,720 --> 00:02:27,160
You see, I... I've had a crush on you ever since we were in our first year. Did you know that?

8
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:29,040
No.

9
00:02:29,540 --> 00:02:32,920
Didn't think so. I hid it so you wouldn't catch on.

10
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:37,580
Please don't let him find out how I feel. That was all I could think about.

11
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:42,400
I'm sure that today will be the last time.

12
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:50,400
But it hit me when I woke up this morning. That from now on, I no longer have to keep on pretending that I don't like you anymore.

13
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:52,700
And that gave me a bit of relief.

14
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:58,820
So it's alright. I have no regrets.

15
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:05,680
Would you mind hearing me out?

16
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:06,680
Sure.

17
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:10,620
You see, I really like the way you play Yamada.

18
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:11,460
Huh?

19
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:16,200
I'm talking about gaming. You're so cool-headed, and you don't blame other people.

20
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:17,760
Uh, huh.

21
00:03:18,180 --> 00:03:23,420
When it comes to PvP games, a lot of other players just lose it, but you never show any signs of that.

22
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:23,980
Huh.

23
00:03:24,760 --> 00:03:27,460
And I really admired how mature you are in that way.

24
00:03:28,340 --> 00:03:28,780
Thanks.

25
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:33,100
I also like how you always look out the window when you're spacing out in the classroom.

26
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:33,860
Hmm?

27
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:37,380
And I could never tell you because I didn't want you to think I was a fangirl.

28
00:03:37,380 --> 00:03:42,440
But the truth is, I always thought you were super good-looking. And I love the way you never show off.

29
00:03:42,440 --> 00:03:47,180
Oh, and I also love your voice. It really calms me down. And I like your quietness.

30
00:03:47,180 --> 00:03:51,080
I like seeing you walk, and also seeing you run. And I like how you're a slow talker.

31
00:03:51,420 --> 00:03:54,520
You know your habit of blinking a lot when you're at a loss? That.

32
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:58,720
I've always liked that, too. And I really like how you're equally kind to everyone.

33
00:04:00,460 --> 00:04:03,980
Over the last three years, I'm sure that a lot of girls have fallen for you.

34
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:08,320
But any way you look at it, I'm sure that I've always liked you more than anyone else.

35
00:04:10,580 --> 00:04:11,480
No question.

36
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:15,860
I'm sure I've always liked you.

37
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:18,680
More than anyone else in the world.

38
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:27,800
I can't really see him.

39
00:04:31,060 --> 00:04:31,900
But...

40
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:34,240
I managed to tell him everything.

41
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:37,820
For so long, it felt like a lead weight.

42
00:04:38,740 --> 00:04:40,880
It's been stressing me out all this time.

43
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:44,500
And that's why...

44
00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:46,680
I absolutely have no regrets.

45
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:50,360
This was such a relief.

46
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:01,680
Tsubaki...

47
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:03,140
I...

48
00:05:03,140 --> 00:05:06,740
I'm really sorry.

49
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:09,800
I can't return your feelings.

50
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:23,260
I'm really sorry.

51
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:24,660
I'm...

52
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:28,100
What's that?

53
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:29,560
On your hand.

54
00:05:30,840 --> 00:05:31,100
Huh?

55
00:05:31,660 --> 00:05:32,260
Oh.

56
00:05:32,940 --> 00:05:33,800
This is...

57
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:38,720
Someone I know did it as a joke.

58
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:40,580
I know.

59
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:42,820
The girl who drew that.

60
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:48,800
She's the girl that...

61
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:51,640
You're in love with.

62
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:52,880
Right?

63
00:05:52,880 --> 00:06:04,580
Yes.

64
00:06:04,580 --> 00:06:04,640
Yes.

65
00:06:09,820 --> 00:06:10,880
Thank you...

66
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:12,380
For having feelings for me.

67
00:06:14,820 --> 00:06:15,860
I'm really sorry.

68
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:18,140
I can't feel the same way about you.

69
00:06:18,140 --> 00:06:22,280
It's all right.

70
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:25,320
Thank you for hearing me out.

71
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:29,000
I'm glad I told you.

72
00:06:31,580 --> 00:06:33,340
I've known all along.

73
00:06:35,220 --> 00:06:37,080
Because I've been watching you.

74
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:40,560
I could tell that you'd changed.

75
00:06:41,060 --> 00:06:42,440
Just a little bit.

76
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:46,100
Even if nobody else noticed.

77
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:52,300
I could tell right away.

78
00:06:52,300 --> 00:06:59,880
It was nice to get all that off my chest.

79
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:02,140
Thanks for making time for me.

80
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:04,760
I'll go...

81
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:05,340
Home now.

82
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:07,100
Okay then.

83
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:07,940
I'll see you at school.

84
00:07:10,440 --> 00:07:11,120
Uh...

85
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:12,160
I'll, um...

86
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:13,000
Walk you home?

87
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:14,660
You don't have your glasses.

88
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:15,620
And it's dark.

89
00:07:15,960 --> 00:07:16,560
It's fine.

90
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:17,980
I can go home by myself.

91
00:07:18,780 --> 00:07:19,220
But...

92
00:07:19,220 --> 00:07:20,420
Don't you worry.

93
00:07:20,420 --> 00:07:22,800
I'm not as weak as I look.

94
00:07:28,580 --> 00:07:29,020
Right.

95
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:32,520
Thank you.

96
00:07:36,940 --> 00:07:39,320
You were so nice to me right to the end.

97
00:07:39,780 --> 00:07:40,820
That made me happy.

98
00:07:41,960 --> 00:07:44,540
That's one of the things I really liked about you.

99
00:07:44,540 --> 00:07:51,560
I really liked you.

100
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:58,440
We'll be going on break soon.

101
00:07:58,600 --> 00:08:00,720
But I don't know what my work schedule will be like.

102
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:02,160
What?

103
00:08:02,220 --> 00:08:02,900
It's too noisy?

104
00:08:03,420 --> 00:08:04,220
Oh, sorry.

105
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:05,720
I'm getting ready to leave the house.

106
00:08:06,220 --> 00:08:07,360
For a meetup with my guilt.

107
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:08,880
No, Mom.

108
00:08:08,980 --> 00:08:09,820
It's not a club.

109
00:08:10,660 --> 00:08:12,240
I explained it before.

110
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:13,600
My gaming friends.

111
00:08:14,220 --> 00:08:15,020
Yeah, that's right.

112
00:08:15,380 --> 00:08:17,340
We're all going out tonight to get dinner together.

113
00:08:17,340 --> 00:08:25,760
Hey, I believe that's her now.

114
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:26,220
See?

115
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:26,840
Over there.

116
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:28,020
Hey, you're right.

117
00:08:28,460 --> 00:08:28,980
Akane!

118
00:08:31,140 --> 00:08:33,140
Mr. Kamata, long time no see.

119
00:08:33,340 --> 00:08:34,520
I'm glad you could come.

120
00:08:34,620 --> 00:08:35,160
Thank you.

121
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:35,600
No, no.

122
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:36,300
Thank you.

123
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:38,420
I really appreciate you inviting me.

124
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:38,700
Kalbi?

125
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:40,360
I could go for some Kalbi.

126
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:41,720
I don't know what's Kalbi too!

127
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:43,500
Hey, Yamata isn't here.

128
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:45,680
Akita will be arriving later.

129
00:08:45,680 --> 00:08:47,040
Hey-o!

130
00:08:47,260 --> 00:08:48,300
You scared me.

131
00:08:48,700 --> 00:08:49,200
Hey-o!

132
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:52,020
Want me to make you some one-on-one time with him?

133
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:55,940
He's been pretty busy, so you don't get to see each other much, right?

134
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:59,080
Darn, I couldn't tell him how I felt the other day.

135
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:01,180
Nah, that's okay.

136
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:03,380
I came here today to have some meat with everyone.

137
00:09:03,700 --> 00:09:04,420
Hello and welcome.

138
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:04,860
That's so.

139
00:09:05,500 --> 00:09:07,400
I have a reservation under Kamata.

140
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:09,260
We've been waiting for you, Mr. Kamata.

141
00:09:09,260 --> 00:09:14,940
And besides, as for Yamata, he seems to be a little tired lately.

142
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:18,240
I think studying for his exams is stressing him out.

143
00:09:18,360 --> 00:09:19,940
I'm quite sure that's not the case.

144
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:23,540
That guy's ready to coast through his entrance exams with flying colors.

145
00:09:23,720 --> 00:09:24,440
No way!

146
00:09:25,340 --> 00:09:28,160
Then I guess I was just imagining things the other day.

147
00:09:28,880 --> 00:09:30,680
This place looks pretty expensive, huh?

148
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:32,160
I bet the meat costs a ton!

149
00:09:32,220 --> 00:09:34,260
Runa, try to keep your voice down, okay?

150
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:35,180
But why?

151
00:09:35,180 --> 00:09:39,260
I guess I should tell you a good friend of mine runs this place.

152
00:09:39,460 --> 00:09:41,900
They actually just had their grand opening the other day.

153
00:09:42,060 --> 00:09:44,060
He's been asking me to come check it out,

154
00:09:44,220 --> 00:09:47,060
so I thought it'd be great to share the experience with my guildmates.

155
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:48,360
Oh, wow, that's amazing!

156
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:50,660
You sure know a lot of people, Mr. Kamata.

157
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:52,180
President Kamata!

158
00:09:53,620 --> 00:09:54,700
It's been a while.

159
00:09:55,380 --> 00:09:56,720
Ah, hello there, Inoue.

160
00:09:56,960 --> 00:09:58,240
You look like you're doing well.

161
00:09:58,300 --> 00:09:59,960
Yes, you look well yourself, sir.

162
00:10:00,540 --> 00:10:02,580
So, how's business these days?

163
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:03,420
We're managing.

164
00:10:03,680 --> 00:10:04,520
Thank you for asking.

165
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:06,120
Oh, hey, President Kamata.

166
00:10:06,340 --> 00:10:07,600
I didn't know you were here.

167
00:10:07,820 --> 00:10:10,620
Professor Obayashi, what a nice surprise seeing you here.

168
00:10:10,780 --> 00:10:12,660
President Kamata, what a coincidence.

169
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:15,220
Director Nagaoka, it's good to see you.

170
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:17,160
Mr. Kamata, what a surprise.

171
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:19,040
You're President Sumiyoshi's wife, right?

172
00:10:19,140 --> 00:10:19,860
Hello there.

173
00:10:20,020 --> 00:10:22,340
Who would have thought we'd all end up here, huh?

174
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:24,700
Oh, man, he knows way too many people.

175
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:26,480
Who even is Mr. Kamata?

176
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:28,360
Hey!

177
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:31,060
We've got a whole room all to ourselves!

178
00:10:31,060 --> 00:10:39,640
This meat is so delicious!

179
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:43,480
And it tastes even better when you're with a lot of people, too, huh?

180
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:47,420
It really is too bad that our newest guild member couldn't share it with us, though.

181
00:10:47,540 --> 00:10:50,400
I did invite her, but it seems like tonight didn't work for her.

182
00:10:50,540 --> 00:10:51,880
She didn't need to come anyway!

183
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:52,640
Huh?

184
00:10:53,380 --> 00:10:54,560
Pardon our interruption.

185
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:58,540
Here you are.

186
00:10:58,740 --> 00:11:01,360
This was sent over by Mr. Inoue from across the hall.

187
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:03,360
This sake is for Mr. Obayashi.

188
00:11:03,520 --> 00:11:05,260
Mr. Nagaoka sent this over.

189
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:07,940
And this comes from Mrs. Sumiyoshi.

190
00:11:10,940 --> 00:11:11,840
Oh, my.

191
00:11:12,020 --> 00:11:13,780
They didn't have to do so much for us.

192
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:14,620
There's even sake!

193
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:15,420
Crazy!

194
00:11:15,780 --> 00:11:18,360
I've never seen other customers send stuff over.

195
00:11:18,620 --> 00:11:19,660
That's so cool!

196
00:11:19,940 --> 00:11:22,420
Someday I want to become a big shot grown-up, too.

197
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:23,580
Just like you are!

198
00:11:23,580 --> 00:11:26,200
What are you going on about?

199
00:11:26,280 --> 00:11:29,040
If you ask me, you're already a fine young man.

200
00:11:29,240 --> 00:11:32,460
After all, I'm only able to grind in the dungeons without a care,

201
00:11:32,640 --> 00:11:36,940
because you've graciously taken on all of the guild management duties for me.

202
00:11:37,900 --> 00:11:41,220
Well, that's because I have your support behind the scenes, Mr. Kamota.

203
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:43,560
Oh, I wouldn't say all that now.

204
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:47,500
The fact of the matter is, you're always creating fun places to hang out in,

205
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:50,460
and introducing me to all kinds of great new friends,

206
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:53,420
so I enjoy each and every day with you.

207
00:11:53,580 --> 00:11:59,040
I hope all of us can keep playing as good friends for as long as time allows.

208
00:12:00,040 --> 00:12:00,900
I hear you!

209
00:12:01,180 --> 00:12:03,760
Bruno wants to keep playing with our guild members forever like always!

210
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,340
Just the current members, though!

211
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:08,720
Forever like always.

212
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:12,060
Yeah, but change is necessary as well, you know.

213
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:15,160
Going forward, our guild will be embracing renewal.

214
00:12:15,240 --> 00:12:16,700
Huh? I'm not here for that!

215
00:12:16,700 --> 00:12:18,820
Why can't we just keep things the way they are?

216
00:12:18,820 --> 00:12:20,500
Change is nothing to be afraid of.

217
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:23,160
Uh, excuse you, that's the meat Bruna was grilling!

218
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:26,700
You may think that, but in truth, dear Runa, since I'm the one who raised you,

219
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:28,620
this Kalbi was actually grilled by meat.

220
00:12:28,620 --> 00:12:29,920
Eita, you suck!

221
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:37,660
Hello and welcome!

222
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:40,480
You're one of Mr. Kamata's party, right?

223
00:12:40,880 --> 00:12:41,920
Follow me if you would.

224
00:12:43,500 --> 00:12:45,760
Oh, hey! The attendant's finally here!

225
00:12:46,300 --> 00:12:47,900
Hakun, you're late!

226
00:12:48,080 --> 00:12:48,400
Yo.

227
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:51,680
Hey, Yamada! Listen to this!

228
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:54,460
You won't believe the fight Bruna was in just now!

229
00:12:54,700 --> 00:12:56,580
You said you could get here sooner, bud!

230
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,500
Hey, you know...

231
00:12:58,500 --> 00:13:03,500
If you all talk at once...

232
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:07,340
Uh-oh. She's already back.

233
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:07,880
Huh?

234
00:13:11,880 --> 00:13:12,080
Hey!

235
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:14,760
If it is Yamada!

236
00:13:17,280 --> 00:13:17,800
What?

237
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:23,540
Uh, can somebody explain why she's so intoxicated?

238
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:28,460
It's my fault for urging her to try a taste of the sake one of my friends gifted to us.

239
00:13:28,700 --> 00:13:30,040
It's not you, Mr. Kamata!

240
00:13:30,420 --> 00:13:33,000
Akane's so wasted because she was guzzling it like crazy!

241
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:37,860
And then she got all hyper and wouldn't stop bugging me, which was seriously annoying!

242
00:13:38,340 --> 00:13:41,660
Akane's the type who gets really cheerful when she's had one too many, huh?

243
00:13:43,100 --> 00:13:44,860
Yamada, I'm leaving the rest to you.

244
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:48,000
If she gets on your nerves, you can leave her on the restroom floor.

245
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:49,180
That's what Bruna did.

246
00:13:49,660 --> 00:13:51,340
No, I couldn't do that.

247
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:52,840
Come on, Akito!

248
00:13:53,140 --> 00:13:54,700
Sit down with us and have some dinner!

249
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:58,200
I'll send Akane home and a taxi later, so no need to worry!

250
00:13:58,340 --> 00:13:59,360
That won't be necessary.

251
00:13:59,540 --> 00:14:02,340
I'll have Akito take Akanechi home, so it's all fine!

252
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:03,120
Really?

253
00:14:03,520 --> 00:14:04,140
Mm-hmm!

254
00:14:04,140 --> 00:14:07,820
Well, you're right, those two have grown rather closely, Lee.

255
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,840
I guess it would be better to leave it to him.

256
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:13,360
Come on!

257
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:16,300
You're so late, Yamada!

258
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:19,800
Yeah, sorry.

259
00:14:21,800 --> 00:14:22,240
YUMMY!

260
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:27,600
Hey, maybe we should just pick someone up off the street now.

261
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:28,300
I bet.

262
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:29,040
Let's go.

263
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:31,360
Are there even any cute girls around now?

264
00:14:37,700 --> 00:14:38,460
Here's water.

265
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:39,220
What the?

266
00:14:39,460 --> 00:14:41,560
Oh crap, was I really just sleeping right here?

267
00:14:41,980 --> 00:14:42,420
Yes.

268
00:14:42,800 --> 00:14:44,340
Wow, I can't believe it.

269
00:14:44,380 --> 00:14:44,800
Me neither.

270
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:48,400
Wow, you got me water!

271
00:14:48,640 --> 00:14:50,700
I was just thinking about how parched I am.

272
00:14:50,760 --> 00:14:52,440
How did you know that I wanted some water?

273
00:14:52,820 --> 00:14:55,100
Because you made a commotion about it in song form.

274
00:14:55,340 --> 00:14:55,540
Ah!

275
00:14:55,900 --> 00:14:56,960
Me oh my!

276
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:58,780
My throat's so dry!

277
00:14:59,040 --> 00:15:01,720
Desert chillin' with the real fun guy!

278
00:15:02,180 --> 00:15:04,640
I'm so sorry for causing you trouble all the time.

279
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:06,440
I'll make sure I don't forget this favor.

280
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:09,380
Whenever I'm drunk, I can barely remember anything afterwards.

281
00:15:09,860 --> 00:15:10,260
Right.

282
00:15:10,500 --> 00:15:11,460
Oh, I'll make a note.

283
00:15:11,640 --> 00:15:13,580
If I leave a record on my phone, I'll be set.

284
00:15:13,580 --> 00:15:15,680
It's okay to forget, so let's just go home.

285
00:15:15,800 --> 00:15:16,420
It's getting late.

286
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:17,720
Oh, you're right.

287
00:15:17,940 --> 00:15:18,940
Just look at the time.

288
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:21,660
Hey, Yamada, you can go on ahead.

289
00:15:21,800 --> 00:15:23,880
Going home with me would be a hassle for you.

290
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:26,080
It's not safe, so I'm taking you.

291
00:15:26,480 --> 00:15:28,180
There are tons of drunks around here.

292
00:15:29,880 --> 00:15:31,140
Other than you, I mean.

293
00:15:43,580 --> 00:15:54,080
Sorry, my heel got stuck in a groove.

294
00:15:54,260 --> 00:15:54,420
Huh?

295
00:15:59,220 --> 00:16:00,020
Uh-oh.

296
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:01,480
Won't come out.

297
00:16:04,360 --> 00:16:08,580
Hey, um, sorry again for causing you so much trouble.

298
00:16:08,580 --> 00:16:10,360
It's really weshed in there.

299
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:16,540
Good.

300
00:16:20,300 --> 00:16:20,900
Got it.

301
00:16:20,900 --> 00:16:43,300
Ready to go?

302
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:44,300
Uh-oh.

303
00:16:45,920 --> 00:16:46,880
Yeah.

304
00:16:58,520 --> 00:16:59,600
Uh-oh.

305
00:16:59,740 --> 00:17:00,140
Well…

306
00:17:00,140 --> 00:17:15,840
Okay, then. I'll be going now. Have a good night.

307
00:17:16,260 --> 00:17:19,080
Thanks so much. Get home safely, okay?

308
00:17:25,220 --> 00:17:25,820
Hey!

309
00:17:27,740 --> 00:17:29,500
Uh, do you...

310
00:17:29,500 --> 00:17:33,760
Uh, I mean, by any chance, do you like me, Yamada?

311
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:44,500
Uh, what? No. It's just... I, uh, I just had a feeling...

312
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:48,500
Because... his hand...

313
00:17:52,140 --> 00:17:54,680
You got me.

314
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:59,820
When his hand was touching mine...

315
00:17:59,820 --> 00:18:01,680
Huh? That means...

316
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:05,140
It seemed like he was telling me that.

317
00:18:09,680 --> 00:18:12,720
I, uh... I'm pretty drunk right now.

318
00:18:13,240 --> 00:18:14,460
Am I talking normally?

319
00:18:15,420 --> 00:18:17,320
What I meant to say is that...

320
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:18,000
I like you.

321
00:18:19,140 --> 00:18:21,480
I... like you, Akane.

322
00:18:23,740 --> 00:18:27,480
And if you don't remember when you wake up in the morning, it's okay.

323
00:18:28,820 --> 00:18:30,000
I'll say it again.

324
00:18:31,800 --> 00:18:32,860
Until you remember.

325
00:18:32,860 --> 00:18:37,120
Have a good night now.

326
00:18:37,120 --> 00:18:54,120
Tomorrow, in the morning, when I wake up...

327
00:18:54,120 --> 00:18:59,340
Is it okay if I call you?

328
00:19:02,460 --> 00:19:04,380
Because I know I'm going to worry...

329
00:19:06,220 --> 00:19:07,380
That all of this...

330
00:19:08,220 --> 00:19:09,000
Was a dream.

331
00:19:14,220 --> 00:19:15,560
That's okay with you.

332
00:19:15,560 --> 00:19:17,620
Right?

333
00:19:25,900 --> 00:19:26,860
I'll call you.

334
00:19:29,860 --> 00:19:30,380
Tomorrow.

335
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:39,800
In the morning, when you wake up.

336
00:19:39,800 --> 00:19:48,140
.

337
00:20:03,200 --> 00:20:04,060
Hey...

338
00:20:04,460 --> 00:20:04,720
Good morning.

339
00:20:05,580 --> 00:20:05,960
Good morning!

340
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:07,440
So?

341
00:20:07,520 --> 00:20:08,660
And then what happened?

342
00:20:08,660 --> 00:20:12,280
How'd the phone call go? I want to know every word you guys said verbatim!

343
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:14,080
Oh, come on. That's private info.

344
00:20:14,460 --> 00:20:16,620
What? You have a boyfriend now, Akane?

345
00:20:16,980 --> 00:20:18,180
Way to go, girl!

346
00:20:18,540 --> 00:20:21,760
Could it be that I'm the only one of us who doesn't have a boyfriend?

347
00:20:22,760 --> 00:20:24,840
Wow, so he's a younger guy!

348
00:20:25,080 --> 00:20:25,320
Yep.

349
00:20:25,880 --> 00:20:28,540
I couldn't date somebody who's younger than me again.

350
00:20:28,980 --> 00:20:29,940
Really? Why not?

351
00:20:30,180 --> 00:20:32,620
It sort of felt like he was looking for a mature woman.

352
00:20:33,100 --> 00:20:35,520
So I wasn't able to let myself depend on him.

353
00:20:35,760 --> 00:20:38,520
He told me he could never get what I was thinking.

354
00:20:38,660 --> 00:20:42,180
So dating a younger guy ended up being pretty hard for me.

355
00:20:42,420 --> 00:20:45,320
But I get the sense that you'll be just fine, Akane.

356
00:20:45,440 --> 00:20:47,420
You say that because it doesn't concern you.

357
00:20:47,500 --> 00:20:48,560
Well, it really doesn't.

358
00:20:49,260 --> 00:20:50,420
Get a grip, Akane.

359
00:20:50,700 --> 00:20:53,440
Would you mind not acting depressed in front of single women like me?

360
00:20:54,320 --> 00:20:54,800
Apologies.

361
00:20:55,720 --> 00:20:57,200
Hmm. Well, it's okay.

362
00:20:57,860 --> 00:21:01,060
I always knew that the two of you would end up together sooner or later.

363
00:21:01,660 --> 00:21:02,400
Did you really?

364
00:21:02,940 --> 00:21:05,160
Yeah, you guys gave off that kind of scent.

365
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:05,840
Scent?

366
00:21:05,840 --> 00:21:10,060
Wait, I didn't really seem like I was throwing myself at Yamada, did I?

367
00:21:10,740 --> 00:21:11,400
No, no.

368
00:21:12,220 --> 00:21:12,500
Mm-hmm.

369
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:13,200
Mm-hmm.

370
00:21:13,760 --> 00:21:15,000
The other way around.

371
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:23,900
So anyway, in other words, what I'm trying to say is, you'll be taking your entrance exams soon, won't you?

372
00:21:24,140 --> 00:21:28,580
I know that you're gonna be totally swamped, so you don't have to worry about me, okay?

373
00:21:29,580 --> 00:21:32,900
I'll do everything in my power to try and not be a burden on you.

374
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:38,000
But still, every once in a while, like when you're tired, I'll be there for you to lean on me, all right?

375
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:40,360
Okay? At least pretend to listen.

376
00:21:41,040 --> 00:21:45,840
No, I was listening. At least until you said that thing about people supporting each other.

377
00:21:46,040 --> 00:21:47,620
That was way back at the beginning.

378
00:21:48,180 --> 00:21:51,360
Yeah, to be honest, it was around that point I started to lose you.

379
00:21:52,560 --> 00:21:59,080
The thing is, Akane, while I was looking at your mouth open and close, I happened to notice that your canine teeth are pointy.

380
00:21:59,460 --> 00:21:59,860
Kay!

381
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:03,540
And while gazing at them, I was thinking they were really cute.

382
00:22:03,740 --> 00:22:04,100
You!

383
00:22:06,040 --> 00:22:06,520
Hmm?

384
00:22:07,220 --> 00:22:08,880
You're teasing me, aren't you?

385
00:22:09,140 --> 00:22:10,280
No, not at all.

386
00:22:12,540 --> 00:22:14,820
This mature woman thing ain't working.

387
00:22:16,500 --> 00:22:17,520
I'll walk you home.

388
00:22:18,180 --> 00:22:18,620
Thanks.

389
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:26,080
By the way...

390
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:26,380
Yes?

391
00:22:27,140 --> 00:22:29,560
What was it that you wanted to say earlier?

392
00:22:29,860 --> 00:22:33,740
Well, um...

393
00:22:33,740 --> 00:22:35,740
Actually...

394
00:22:35,740 --> 00:22:42,880
I was trying to tell you I wanted to hold hands when we're walking.

395
00:22:46,620 --> 00:22:47,180
Oh.

396
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:48,880
I'm sorry.

397
00:22:55,280 --> 00:22:57,680
Wasn't that a cryptic way of telling me, though?

398
00:22:57,680 --> 00:23:00,100
I'll try working on that.

399
00:23:00,760 --> 00:23:01,800
That would be great.

400
00:23:05,980 --> 00:23:07,160
What is this?

401
00:23:07,560 --> 00:23:08,280
A shoe?

402
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:11,300
It must be a shoe, I guess.

403
00:23:13,020 --> 00:23:14,940
Does this even function as a shoe?

404
00:23:14,940 --> 00:23:16,700
Nah.

405
00:23:16,700 --> 00:23:19,900
It turned out like that because it malfunctioned.

406
00:23:21,020 --> 00:23:23,320
If you're going to crumple up on the ground,

407
00:23:24,520 --> 00:23:26,900
shouldn't you wear normal shoes that are functional?

408
00:23:29,400 --> 00:23:30,820
I just don't get them.

409
00:23:31,820 --> 00:23:32,820
Women...

410
00:23:32,820 --> 00:23:34,780
Are you okay?

411
00:23:34,780 --> 00:23:34,800
Are you okay?

412
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:35,820
Are you okay?

413
00:23:35,820 --> 00:24:05,800
Thank you.

